G=[("How to find fully funded scholarships","Start with official government portals, then university scholarship pages, then supervisor-funded positions.",["Check each provider's eligibility on its own website","Note nationality, degree level and language rules","Record deadlines in one place"]),("Government vs professor-funded scholarships","Government awards are competitive and have fixed cycles. Professor-funded positions depend on a supervisor's grant and are often more flexible on timing.",["Government: central application, set deadline","Professor-funded: direct contact with the supervisor","Many applicants pursue both"]),("How to contact an international research supervisor","Write a short, specific email showing you have read their work.",["Clear subject line","Two sentences on your background and one on fit","Attach a concise CV","Follow up once after about two weeks"]),("How to write a strong academic CV","Lead with education and research, keep it factual and easy to scan.",["Education with dates and grades","Research experience and publications","Skills and relevant awards","Two pages or fewer at early stages"]),("Preparing a statement of purpose","Explain why this subject, why this programme and why you are ready.",["Be specific about interests","Link past work to future goals","Avoid generic praise of the university"]),("Scholarship application document checklist","Requirements differ, so start from the official list.",["Passport and transcripts as required by the provider","Degree certificates and CV","Recommendation letters","Language test results where required"]),("Finding funded PhD research positions","Search university vacancy pages and research job boards, and contact supervisors directly.",["Match your thesis topic to lab output","Check whether the position includes a salary or stipend","Confirm language and start-date requirements"]),("Scholarship application mistakes to avoid","Most rejections come from avoidable problems.",["Missing the deadline or documents","Ignoring eligibility rules","Sending identical emails to many professors","Weak or unclear statements"]),("How to prepare for a scholarship interview","Know your application and your research story.",["Rehearse a two-minute introduction","Be ready to discuss your thesis and future plans","Prepare questions for the panel"]),("Planning your study abroad application timeline","Begin early; many cycles open 8 to 12 months before the start of study.",["Research and shortlist first","Prepare tests and documents next","Apply, then follow up","Always confirm dates on the official site"])]
